  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A refractory high-entropy alloy containing a significant amount of Nb could become superconducting at cryogenic temperatures.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A disordered solid-solution structure may promote electron pairing in an Nb-containing RHEA.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb, Ta, Ti, and Zr can be constituents of a refractory concentrated alloy.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11077685::chunk::001::introduction::c842910f4e"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed Nb-Ta-Ti-Zr-containing alloy is a single-phase material with near-equiatomic proportions.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11077685::chunk::001::introduction::c842910f4e"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A superconducting transition in the proposed alloy may be detectable below 10 K.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The high-entropy alloy has a disordered FCC or BCC solid-solution structure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The disordered solid solution may reduce scattering from grain boundaries.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An appropriate disordered alloy composition may create an environment conducive to Cooper-pair formation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At low temperatures, Cooper pairing may occur in the metallic matrix of the alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cooper pairing would produce a superconducting phase with zero electrical resistance.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed superconducting phase would expel magnetic fields through the Meissner effect.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Below a critical temperature, the alloy is expected to show zero resistance and measurable magnetic-field expulsion.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Above the critical temperature, the alloy behaves as a conventional metal.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At room temperature, the alloy has metallic conduction without superconducting behavior.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The superconducting properties may be sensitive to minor compositional variations and phase purity.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Low-temperature decomposition products such as sigma phases could suppress or alter the superconducting transition.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb is a known component of superconducting alloys.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The exact critical temperature cannot be predicted without experimental verification.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
